Your rules for this feature, as the builders will follow them (each one applies to every case like it, not just the example):
  1. Whenever a refund is worked out for returned items, the amount is what the customer actually paid for those items: item price times quantity for the returned items, minus any discount code, with the time rules applied. For example, a 5,000 rupee jacket bought for 3,500 rupees with a coupon gets a refund of 3,500 rupees.
  2. Whenever a refund works out to a part-rupee amount, pay the amount rounded down to the whole rupee, so the shop keeps the part-rupee. For example, 1,249.60 rupees is paid as 1,249 rupees.
  3. Whenever a refund is requested and the goods did not arrive damaged and the order is not final-sale, handle it by the normal refund rules if the request is made up to 30 days after delivery. If it is made 31 or more days after delivery, refuse it and refund nothing. This applies to every kind of item, including gift cards, custom-embroidered items and fresh food, because the owner has no special rule for them.
  4. Whenever the goods arrived damaged and the refund request is made up to 90 days after delivery, refund the full amount, including the delivery (shipping) fee. If the goods arrived damaged and the request is made more than 90 days after delivery, refund nothing. This applies to final-sale orders too.
  5. Whenever an order is marked final-sale and the goods did not arrive damaged, refund nothing.
  6. Whenever a customer returns goods because they changed their mind (or for any reason other than 'damaged'), refund the item price in full with no deduction, and do not refund the delivery charge. For example, Arjun's 2,000 rupee shoes with 150 rupees delivery get a refund of 2,000 rupees.
  7. Whenever a refund request has the reason 'damaged', apply the damaged-goods rule. Whenever the reason is 'wrong item sent', 'delivered 10 days late', 'other' or blank, treat it exactly like a changed-mind refund.
  8. Whenever a refund is calculated, never refund tax or gift-wrap fees. Refund the delivery fee only if the goods were damaged.
  9. Whenever an approved refund is for an order paid by card, return it to that card. Whenever an approved refund is for an order paid with store credit, return it as store credit.
  10. Whenever an order has not been delivered, there is nothing to refund until it is delivered. Refunds are only handled for delivered orders.
